      "side": 1,
      "message": "Calls to connectToCell must be paired with calls to disconnectFromCell. Otherwise cellular data will remain connected for all subsequent tests.\n\nI\u0027ve seen several CLs forget to do this, which suggests that the name and/or the shape of the API are difficult to use. Maybe rename connectToCell to requestCellular, and disconnectFromCell to releaseCellRequest?\n\nMight want to put releaseCellRequest into tearDown, too. Or, we could add a tearDown method to CtsNetUtils that calls releaseCellRequest. Then make sure that any test using CtsNetUtils calls mCtsNetUtils.tearDown() in tearDown().\n\nOnce we have this, we could use it to ensure that any call to ensureWifiConnected() or ensureWifiDisconnected() is undone by tearDown().",
